# act (https://github.com/nektos/act) configuration for running prx's GitHub
# Actions workflows locally. Read automatically by `act` from the repo root.
# Driven by `bun run ci:act` (packages/prx/scripts/local-ci-act); see
# docs/local-ci.md for the full local-CI story (incl. Lima/Colima on macOS).

# Map the `ubuntu-latest` runner to a catthehacker image. These images bundle
# the tooling GitHub's hosted runners ship with (node, git, etc.); the bare
# `act-*` images stay small and our workflows install bun via setup-bun anyway.
# Pinned to the 22.04 tag for reproducibility — bump deliberately, like the
# action SHAs in .github/workflows.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Quieter, deterministic output for a local run.
--rm

# Apple Silicon note: if an action assumes amd64 and fails, re-run with
#   bun run ci:act -- --container-architecture linux/amd64
# (emulated, slower). Left out here so native arm64 VMs/hosts run natively.
